     I don't know how it works under Windows, but for Unix (and also
for VMS) what you've said is wrong.  The code is essentially
  dir =3D getenv("NETHACKDIR")
  if (dir =3D=3D NULL) dir =3D getenv("HACKDIR")
  if (argv[1] =3D=3D "-d") dir =3D argv[2]
(That's not the actual code [particularly the string comparison :-]
but the sequence is similar.  -d on the command line overrides HACKDIR
and whichever of them gets used is recorded with the same variable so
they operate identically.)

     Perhaps you're not setting the environment variable in a way that
nethack can actually see it.


